wserMain`).\\n\\nThe trigger is the named session partition: with the **default** session the identical call rejects cleanly with `NotFoundError: No device selected`. `navigator.bluetooth.requestDevice()` crashes the same way. Registering a `select-usb-device` handler that cancels the request (`event.preventDefault(); callback()`) does **not** prevent the crash — the fault happens in native code before the JS handler resolves.\\n\\n```\\nException Type:    EXC_BAD_ACCESS (SIGSEGV)\\nException Subtype: KERN_INVALID_ADDRESS at 0x0000000000000100\\nTriggered by Thread: 0  CrBrowserMain\\n\\nThread 0 Crashed:: CrBrowserMain\\n0  Electron Framework  v8::CppHeap::Create(...)\\n1  Electron Framework  node::PrincipalRealm::...\\n```\\n\\n(Symbol names are nearest-export approximations from a release build; the fault is inside V8 / cppgc internals during device-chooser setup.)\\n\\nRegarding the Chromium question above: the trigger is an Electron-specific `webPreferences.partition` (named session), which has no web-page-settable equivalent in stock Chrome, so I can't reproduce it directly there. The crash itself is in the Chromium-layer device-chooser path, so a Chromium root cause is still possible.\\n\\n### Testcase Gist URL\\n\\nhttps://gist.github.com/boutetnico/cd2005b668f680b47abab2056b3fccc6\\n\\n### Additional Information\\n\\nThe only difference between the crashing and non-crashing runs is a single `webPreferences.partition` value. In the gist, `main.js` calls `requestDevice()` from the main process via `webContents.executeJavaScript(code, /* userGesture */ true)` on `did-finish-load`; flipping the `USE_DEFAULT_SESSION` constant to `true` gives the non-crashing control case. No device or hardware is required — the crash happens while opening the device chooser.\\n\\nReproduced identically on:\\n\\n| Electron | Chromium | Result |\\n| --- | --- | --- |\\n| 41.10.0 | 146 | SIGSEGV |\\n| 41.10.2 | 146 | SIGSEGV |\\n| 43.1.1 | 150 | SIGSEGV |\\n\",\n  \"form\": \"bug\",\n  \"labels_already_applied\": [],\n  \"author_association\": \"NONE\",\n  \"opened\": \"2026-07-17T19:48:41Z\"\n },\n \"form_fields\": {\n  \"electron_version\": \"43.1.1\",\n  \"os\": \"macOS\",\n  \"last_known_working\": \"Unknown — every version I tested reproduces (41.10.0, 41.10.2, 43.1.1); not bisected further back.\",\n  \"testcase_gist_url\": \"https://gist.github.com/boutetnico/cd2005b668f680b47abab2056b3fccc6\"\n },\n \"repro\": {\n  \"gist\": true,\n  \"other_repo_link\": false,\n  \"code_blocks\": 1\n },\n \"bot_already\": {\n  \"asked_for_supported_version\": false,\n  \"need_repro_label\": false\n },\n \"issues_linked_by_reporter\": [],\n \"component_hints\": [\n  {\n   \"label\": \"component/deviceAccess\",\n   \"matched\": [\n    \"navigator.usb\",\n    \"select-usb-device\",\n    \"requestdevice\"\n   ],\n   \"in_title\": true\n  },\n  {\n   \"label\": \"component/session\",\n   \"matched\": [\n    \"partition\"\n   ],\n   \"in_title\": true\n  },\n  {\n   \"label\": \"component/webcontents\",\n   \"matched\": [\n    \"webcontents\",\n    \"did-finish-load\",\n    \"executejavascript\"\n   ],\n   \"in_title\": false\n  },\n  {\n   \"label\": \"component/v8\",\n   \"matched\": [\n    \"v8\",\n    \"heap\"\n   ],\n   \"in_title\": false\n  },\n  {\n   \"label\": \"component/bluetooth\",\n   \"matched\": [\n    \"bluetooth\"\n   ],\n   \"in_title\": false\n  },\n  {\n   \"label\": \"component/build\",\n   \"matched\": [\n    \"e build\"\n   ],\n   \"in_title\": false\n  }\n ],\n \"redirect_hints\": {\n  \"upstream\": [\n   \"chromium\"\n  ]\n },\n \"similar_candidates\": [\n  {\n   \"number\": 50790,\n   \"opened\": \"2026-04-07\",\n   \"score\": 74.9,\n   \"title\": \"EXC_BREAKPOINT / pointer authentication trap in CFRetain during async OSR paint handler (macOS arm64, 41.1.1)\",\n   \"shared_terms\": [\n    \"internals\",\n    \"principalrealm\",\n    \"cppgc\",\n    \"crbrowsermain\",\n    \"triggered\",\n    \"callback\",\n    \"framework\",\n    \"exception\"\n   ],\n   \"already_linked_by_reporter\": false,\n   \"excerpt\": \"## Preflight Checklist ## Electron Version 41.1.1 ## What operating system(s) are you using? macOS ## Operating System Version macOS 26.4 (build 25E246) — Darwin 25.4.0, ARM64 (native, not translated) ## What arch are you using? arm64 (Apple Silicon — MacBookPro18,3) ## Last Known Working Electron Version Unknown — first observed on 41.x ## Does the issue also appear in Chromium / Google Chrome? N\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"number\": 51574,\n   \"opened\": \"2026-05-09\",\n   \"score\": 65.1,\n   \"title\": \"Crash (SIGSEGV) on right-click in -webkit-app-region: drag on macOS 26\",\n   \"shared_terms\": [\n    \"subtype\",\n    \"kern_invalid_address\",\n    \"exc_bad_access\",\n    \"sigsegv\",\n    \"crbrowsermain\",\n    \"main.js\",\n    \"framework\",\n    \"crashed\"\n   ],\n   \"already_linked_by_reporter\": false,\n   \"excerpt\": \"## Description Right-clicking on an element with `-webkit-app-region: drag` in a `titleBarStyle: 'hidden'` window causes a SIGSEGV crash (null pointer dereference at address 0x0) on macOS 26 (Tahoe, build 25C56). The crash occurs inside `[ElectronNSWindow sendEvent:]` → `[super sendEvent:]` when processing `NSEventTypeRightMouseDown`. The `sendEvent` override temporarily disables draggable regions\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"number\": 51351,\n   \"opened\": \"2026-04-27\",\n   \"score\": 64.6,\n   \"title\": \"MAS-sandboxed Electron 41.3.0 crashes at startup on macOS 26.x with `EXC_BREAKPOINT brk 0` deep in V8 (`ThreadPoolSingleThreadForegroundBlocking0` thread)\",\n   \"shared_terms\": [\n    \"nearest\",\n    \"fault\",\n    \"named\",\n    \"symbol\",\n    \"triggered\",\n    \"hardware\",\n    \"framework\",\n    \"crashed\"\n   ],\n   \"already_linked_by_reporter\": false,\n   \"excerpt\": \"### Expected Behavior A correctly-signed, MAS-sandboxed Electron app should launch normally on macOS 26.x when delivered through TestFlight or the Mac App Store. ### Actual Behavior App crashes at startup with `EXC_BREAKPOINT (SIGTRAP)` / `brk 0` on a thread named `ThreadPoolSingleThreadForegroundBlocking0`. Crash occurs ~2 seconds after launch on Electron 36, ~13 seconds on Electron 41 — gets fur\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"number\": 52295,\n   \"opened\": \"2026-07-09\",\n   \"score\": 56.9,\n   \"title\": \"[Bug]: macOS main process crashes with NSInvalidArgumentException when notification icon attachment creation fails\",\n   \"shared_terms\": [\n    \"crbrowsermain\",\n    \"reproduced\",\n    \"identical\",\n    \"triggered\",\n    \"callback\",\n    \"framework\",\n    \"crashed\",\n    \"exception\"\n   ],\n   \"already_linked_by_reporter\": false,\n   \"excerpt\": \"### Expected Behavior If creating the `UNNotificationAttachment` for the notification icon fails (e.g. the image cannot be persisted to disk), the notification should be delivered without the icon, and the app should not crash. ### Actual Behavior The browser process crashes with an uncaught Objective-C exception before the notification is delivered: ``` *** Terminating app due to uncaught excepti\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"number\": 51576,\n   \"opened\": \"2026-05-10\",\n   \"score\": 56.8,\n   \"title\": \"Crash (SIGSEGV) on right-click in -webkit-app-region: drag on macOS 26 (Tahoe)\",\n   \"shared_terms\": [\n    \"kern_invalid_address\",\n    \"exc_bad_access\",\n    \"sigsegv\",\n    \"main.js\",\n    \"framework\",\n    \"exception\",\n    \"thread\",\n    \"calls\"\n   ],\n   \"already_linked_by_reporter\": false,\n   \"excerpt\": \"### Expected Behavior Right-clicking on an element with -webkit-app-region: drag in a titleBarStyle: 'hidden' window should show a context menu or do nothing. It should not crash. ### Actual Behavior The app crashes with SIGSEGV (EXC_BAD_ACCESS, KERN_INVALID_ADDRESS at 0x0). The crash occurs inside [ElectronNSWindow sendEvent:] which temporarily disables draggable regions via SetDisableDraggableRe\"\n  }\n ],\n \"similar_search\": \"BM25 ove